     "type": "output_text",
     "text": "The model below uses **A0 as the context function**, as requested, and A1\u2013A5 as its child functions. In strict FIPS 183 diagram notation, the context diagram is **A-0**, containing function A0; the decomposition diagram is **A0**.\n\nHardware tag names identify physical I/O. The required logical identifiers are preserved exactly: **start, stop, settled, r, fill_valve, discharge_valve**. In particular, `settled` and `r` are derived internally, not additional physical inputs.\n\n| Node | Function | Inputs | Controls | Outputs | Mechanisms |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **A0** | **Control tank level** | StartCommand button signal; StopCommand button signal; LevelMeter register value | Initial step 0; start-event semantics; stop priority; target \\(h_{sp}=h_{target}=0.8h_{span}\\); overfill limit \\(h_{max}=0.9h_{span}\\); tolerance \\(\\varepsilon=0.02h_{span}\\); hold time \\(t_h=10\\,s\\); PID gains \\(K_p,T_i,T_d\\); PID output limits of 0\u2013100%; integration-suspension rule during clamping; discharge opening of 40%; FULL_SCALE = 1000; I/O mapping and driver Scale = 100 | FillValve register command; DischargeValve register command; logical output indications `fill_valve` and `discharge_valve` | OpenPLC Runtime and PLC program; Modbus TCP connection; Factory I/O driver and analog Level Control scene |\n| **A1** | **Acquire commands and scale level measurement** | StartCommand signal at %IX100.0; StopCommand signal at %IX100.1; LevelMeter value at %IW100 | I/O mapping; scan timing; rising-edge definition of `start`; FULL_SCALE = 1000; measuring span \\(h_{span}\\); level conversion \\(h=(\\text{LevelMeter}/\\text{FULL_SCALE})h_{span}\\) | `start` event, TRUE only in the scan of a button press; `stop` condition; measured level \\(h\\) | OpenPLC input processing; edge-detection logic; Modbus TCP interface; Factory I/O driver |\n| **A2** | **Evaluate level conditions and settling duration** | Measured level \\(h\\) | Target \\(h_{target}=h_{sp}\\);